  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "Supplying the standard quasi-polynomial and Ehrhart background still leaves a genuine source-local mechanism: the cumulative growth function is decomposed coset-wise into shifted dilations of the rational growth polytope, and the exact deviation hypothesis C1+C2<1 is what makes a single interval of admissible alpha available. The required core proves the shifted-dilation Ehrhart theorem for a non-central dilation centre, using an integer-point transform over the cone of the polytope, half-open fundamental domains, and a triangulation reduction to simplices. Together with the exact constants in the hypothesis that core is above ordinary PhD qualifying material in Ehrhart theory and periodic-graph growth.",
